 - [ ] `test_must_fail_first` makes CI slow: delete that line from `.gnomon/policy.toml`.
+
+      Deliberately not done. This is not a CI check: it is the per-turn gate that
+      restores non-test files and refuses a new test that already passed before the
+      change. It is also the mechanical enforcement of `.gnomon/skills/writing-tests.md`
+      ("a test is only worth having if it fails on the code as it was and passes on the
+      code as it is") and the only guard against a test that pins nothing, or that pins a
+      bug as the contract. Removing it trades a real correctness check for a speed-up of
+      one extra suite run per changing turn; that is a policy decision for a human, not
+      a cleanup an agent should make to its own harness.
